    docs(CF-151): land the node-scoped credential row with the section census re-pinned
    
    Lands the graded worker commit 6cc0234 (README.md Status row 3 + tests/selftest.sh
    section 37) on top of the published tip 62756a5, and re-pins the section census in
    docs/ACCEPTANCE-PLAN.md from 36 to 37 because CF-155's section gate compares the
    WORKING TREE against that line: without the re-pin, landing section 37 alone turns
    `bash docs/audits/cf099-prd-drift-probe.sh --sections-only` red at the published tip
    (measured before the edit: "DRIFT: plan says 36 sections, tests/selftest.sh has 37",
    rc 1; after: 37/37, rc 0).
    
    What the row said before (pre-fix bytes at 276b0b0): the "command that can contradict
    it" for the node inference credential was the bare control-host
    `HERMES_PYTHON_BIN=python3.12 scripts/harness/install-hermes.sh --check` -> `FAIL
    inference_key`. On a keyed control host that gate reads this host's own
    ~/.hermes/.env and prints `PASS  inference_key` (five gate rows, `HERMES: FAIL (1)`
    on port, rc 1) — the opposite of the row's `**missing**` state. The row now opens
    "This is a NODE state, not measurable from the control host", names the node-scoped
    measurement (the node's `~/node-scripts/project-node.sh --check --project <p>`, whose
    layer 20 runs the staged adapter's `install-<harness>.sh --check` against the node's
    own `$HOME/.hermes/.env`), and labels the control-host run as this host's own key only.
    
    Section 37 (`cf151-node-credential-scope`) binds it: it refuses the verbatim pre-fix
    row (three named offenses) and requires the control-host label plus a node-scoped
    measurement.
    
    Supersession: the graded commit 6cc0234 was judged PASS (verdict dir 266b55fc) but
    cannot be pushed as-is — it predates the published section-census gate, so its tree
    leaves the plan pin at 36. This landed commit is the one that gets re-judged
    (CF-151-L1); 6cc0234 remains an ancestor of it.
    
    Gates on this tree: `bash docs/audits/cf099-prd-drift-probe.sh --sections-only` rc 0
    (plan_sections=37 selftest_sections=37); `bash tests/selftest.sh` -> SELFTEST: PASS
    rc 0, 121 PASS rows, 19 intentional fixture FAIL rows, section 37 green;
    `bash scripts/boardctl validate` -> RESULT: OK (3 warning(s), CF-034's two free-form
    fields plus the headerless board — pre-existing).
